{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was a member of the House of Toulouse and the grandson of Raymond II Count of Tripoli. Raymond III succeeded his father Raymond II as Count of Tripoli after his death in 1152. He was only a child at the time and the regency was held by his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\nRaymond III was born around 1140. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father was killed in 1152 during a battle with the Banu Ammar emirs of Tripoli. After his father's death Raymond III succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. He was only a child at the time and the regency was held by his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem.\n\nRaymond III came of age in 1155 and took control of the county. He was a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played an important role in the politics of the kingdom. In 1157 he participated in the Siege of Shaizar alongside King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. The siege was unsuccessful and the Crusaders were forced to retreat.\n\n*Marriage and Family*\nRaymond III married Hodierna of Jerusalem's niece Eschiva of Bures. The marriage was likely arranged by King Amalric I of Jerusalem who was Hodierna's brother. Eschiva was the daughter of William of Bures and Eschiva of Saint Omer. Raymond III and Eschiva had no children together.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin. He was captured by Saladin's forces and later executed. The County of Tripoli was inherited by his godson Raymond IV of Tripoli who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.245502233505249}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.07054182887077332}, {"token